# Exceptions & Errors

## Types

| Class | File | When thrown |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `BlingApiException` | `src/exceptions/bling-api.exception.ts` | Bling returns a structured error body (`IDefaultErrorResponse`) |
| `BlingInternalException` | `src/exceptions/bling-internal.exception.ts` | Network/transport failure or empty error payload |

## API Error Shape

`src/entities/@shared/interfaces/error.interface.ts` defines `IDefaultErrorResponse` with nested `error.type`, `error.message`, `error.description`, and optional `error.fields` for validation errors.

`BlingApiException`:

- Sets `Error.message` from `response.error.description`.
- Exposes full payload via readonly `response` getter.

## Handling Flow

`BlingRepository.defaultCatchBehavior` and `OAuthClient` interpret axios errors into the same two exception types. Entities propagate exceptions; they do not wrap or swallow them.

Consumers should catch `BlingApiException` for business/API errors and `BlingInternalException` for connectivity issues.

## Entity Documentation

Every public entity method documents:

```
@throws {BlingApiException|BlingInternalException}
```

Follow wording in `src/entities/contatos/index.ts` or `src/entities/nfes/index.ts`.

## Extension Rules

- Do not introduce new exception types unless the library needs a distinct handling contract.
- Do not parse error bodies in entity methods.
- If Bling adds error fields, extend `IDefaultErrorResponse` in `@shared` rather than per-entity duplicates.
